<Base title="About — labs.walerys.app" description="Who writes this notebook and why it's called labs.">
  <article class="prose">
    <h1>About</h1>
    <p>
      Automation, integrations, experiments with home and network. Professionally I work
      with systems; privately I take them apart to understand how they work.
    </p>

    <h2 id="the-name">Why labs?</h2>
    <p>
      Because this is a laboratory, not a product. Posts are notes from experiments: what
      I tried, what worked, what surprised me. Nothing here is a dissertation — sometimes
      it will be wrong, and a correction becomes another post.
    </p>

    <h2>The site</h2>
    <p>
      <a href="https://astro.build/">Astro</a> builds it, <a href="https://actions.github.com/">GitHub
      Actions</a> checks and ships it, and <a href="https://pages.github.com/">GitHub Pages</a>
      serves the finished blog. Changing the site is a commit, not manual file uploads.
    </p>
    <p>
      The domain is registered with <a href="https://www.ovhcloud.com/">OVH</a>.
      I use my own DNS server and hosting with domain support on
      <a href="https://www.mydevil.net/">myDevil</a>. Those are separate pieces of
      infrastructure — the blog itself is published on GitHub Pages.
    </p>
  </article>
</Base>
